{{/*
  DESIGN-OWNED ARTIFACT — settings.tmpl · package v3.23.1 · WORKFLOW.md v4
  Source of truth: examples/console/Settings.jsx + Sources.jsx + Integrations.jsx · shots 17–18.
  Replaces templates_settings.go wholesale (defines "settings" + "forbidden" + one
  "settings-<tab>" per section). The repo's "scantrigger" define is still called as-is (it stays
  repo-authored until its own map item). "sevbadge" is NOT used here — severity never appears on
  settings surfaces.
  Reconciliations (SPEC-CHANGE #26, ruled):
  #26a nav — the spec sidebar (grouped SettingsNav, 210px, sticky) replaces the tabs row;
    navigation stays ?tab= links. Groups: Scanning (scans, vantages) · Access (sso, team,
    sessions, audit) · Discovery (sources, aperture) · Instance (instance) · Delivery (channels,
    integrations{{/**/}}, messages, delivery). Integrations gated by integrationsEnabled.
  #26b scans — the tab is the queue read (in-flight fan-out + jobs, recent dispatches) plus the
    relocated cold tier (#21d), spec-styled. The mock's "Recurring intent" config card and the
    schedule Calendar are DEFERRED — no operator-editable scan-config store exists; nothing is
    fabricated (ADR-0110). They stay in the spec as the target for a future config store.
  #26c vantages — spec VantageCards replace the table; each provisioned prober renders its real
    lifecycle (awaiting key → install key (inverted CodeBlock + copy) → pinned + platform); the
    mock's 3-step wizard maps onto that lifecycle, not onto client steps. The egress note links
    /scope (no declare-egress POST exists). #26d the preferred-vantage Combobox is DEFERRED (no
    default-vantage store).
  #26e sso — OIDC stands (ADR-0113); the mock's SAML metadata drop, claim MappingEditor, SP
    certificates and require-SSO switch predate it and RETIRE. The provider table (+ edit
    disclosure), add form, and linked-identities table render spec-styled.
  #26f channels — class checkboxes and badges render from .ClassOptions / .Classes (the store's
    vocabulary), never a hardcoded set.
  #26g messages — the tab keeps the repo's full store list (cause · class · headline · census ·
    delivery receipts · mark-read), spec-styled with the inbox treatments; /inbox stays the
    primary surface.
  #26h delivery — the mock's error/skeleton/retry states are client-runtime affordances and drop;
    the server renders data or the honest empty. Retention dials stay.
  #26i team — invite keeps the repo's link flow (no mail in build): role pick → one-time join
    link with the shown-once warning + copy. Member rows render initial-avatars derived from the
    username (no new datum). Dialogs stay PRG (?role= ?reenroll= ?remove= ?invite=1) with the
    spec panel; remove keeps typed-confirm (JS-gated, server validates).
  #26j integrations — the spec catalogue maps PRG: cat/q = GET params, tile click = ?view={id}
    drawer, install/remove/test = POSTs (/settings/integrations, alias or BUILD).
  #39 integrations — the installed drawer binds a delivery Channel (nullable): a "Delivery channel"
    <select> POSTs /settings/integrations/channel {id,channel}; Send test is gated on the binding —
    disabled with "Connect a channel to test" when unbound (no POST), POSTs /settings/integrations/test
    when bound. An integration references a Channel, it is not one (migration 20600).
  Holes per section are documented inline at each define.
*/}}
